They will kill him, and on the third day, he will rise from the dead." The disciples were filled with great sorrow. Jesus pays the tribute to the throne
Jesus and his disciples arrived in Capernaum. There, tax collectors came to Peter and asked him, "Does not your teacher pay the temple tax?"
Yes, he does, he answered. And when Peter entered the house, Jesus was the first to speak. "What do you think, Simon?" he asked. "From whom do the kings of the earth collect customs and taxes, their own sons or foreigners?"
Peter answered, "From others." And Jesus said to him, "Then the children will be free."
But we do not want to anger them. Go to the lake and cast your line. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. There you will find the exact coin you need. Take it and give it to them as a tax for you and me.
